intrigue|PASS: The unsigned letter arouses curiosity rather than a conspiratorial noun sense; intrigued person/intriguing cause grammar and museum example are coherent.
pessimistic|PASS: Negative expectation is distinguished from certainty; the clear forecast contrast remains coherent and pessimistic about chances translates as bi quan.
stubborn|PASS: Refusal to change a decision differs from a stain resisting removal; Vietnamese captures the person/object distinction, including the organizer refusing to postpone.
wash|PASS: Water-cleaning hands, laundering curtains and countable washing occasion have supported ordinals; all three translations retain their objects and wash inflection/countability.
down|PASS: Lower movement differs from motion along a lane; the prepositional example need not slope, and both Vietnamese route and climbing contexts are faithful.
